(a) moneys deposited with the University by any person, wherever by the conditions of such deposit any such sum has become repayable ;

(b) moneys collected and credited to the Funds of the University in error ;

(c) moneys payable by the University under any judgement or order of court ;

(d) moneys expended by the University m instituting or defending legal proceedings ; and

(e) expenditure arising out of any property or moneys referred to in section 40. Form of 39. The annual and supplementary estimates shall be prepared in such Estimates. form and shall contain such information as the Council may direct. Power of the 40. (1) The Council may on behalf of the University accept by way Council to of grant, gift, testamentary disposition or otherwise, property and accept gifts. moneys in aid of the finances of the University on such conditions as it may determine.

(2) The Bursar shall keep and maintain registers of all donations to the University including the names of donors and any special conditions on which any donation may have been given. Properly given 41. All property, moneys or funds given for any specific purposes for specific shall be applied and administered in accordance with the purposes for purposes to be which they may have been given and shall be separately accounted for . separately accounted for. Form of 42. Any contract involving the expenditure by the University of contracts. more than five hundred dollars shall be in writing, signed on behalf of the University by a person acting under the expressed or implied authority of the University ; Provided that any contract (other than a contract referred to in subsection (2) of section 54) involving expenditure by the University of more than ten thousand dollars, and any contract which if made between private persons would be required by law to be under seal shall be executed by affixing thereto the common seal of the University. Dividends 43. No dividend or bonus shall be paid and no gift or division of prohibited. money shall be made by or on behalf of the University to or among any of its members except by way of prize, reward or special grant or as part of the terms and conditions of service of staff of the University. Audit. 44. (1) The accounts of the University shall be audited annually by auditors appointed by the Council.

(2) The audited accounts, with any observation made thereon by the auditors, shall be presented to the Minister of Finance.

STUDENTS OF THE UNIVERSITY Admission of 45. A student shall not be admitted to any course of study in the students. University unless he has satisfied the entry requirements prescribed for the course of study.

